<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
    <Cosmere.System.Scadrial.Def.AllomanticAbilityDef ParentName="AbstractToggleSelfBurnAbility">
        <defName>Cosmere_Scadrial_Ability_ZincAura</defName>
        <label>rioting aura</label>
        <description>The Rioter subtly fans the emotional flames of all nearby minds.

Friendly individuals feel surges of courage and determination, sharpening their reflexes and fueling their will to fight.
Hostile or neutral targets grow tense, anxious, or unstable — their emotions stretched toward breaking.</description>
        <metal>Zinc</metal>
        <canUseWhileAsleep>true</canUseWhileAsleep>
        <hediff>Cosmere_Scadrial_Hediff_ZincAura</hediff>
        <maxPower>2</maxPower>
    </Cosmere.System.Scadrial.Def.AllomanticAbilityDef>
    <!-- One push, not a channel. AbstractToggleTargetBurnAbility runs
         Cosmere_Scadrial_Job_MaintainAllomanticTarget, which walks the caster to the target and
         holds them there - a leash, on the one mechanic built to have none. -->
    <Cosmere.System.Scadrial.Def.AllomanticAbilityDef ParentName="AbstractTargetBurnAbility">
        <defName>Cosmere_Scadrial_Ability_ZincTarget</defName>
        <!-- Vanilla's ability job, not the allomantic one. AbstractTargetBurnAbility runs
             CastAllomanticAbilityAtTarget, which is the iron and steel driver - it calls MoveThing
             and physically throws whatever you aimed at, and never runs a single ability comp.
             Rioting somebody sent them flying and took hold of nothing. CastAbilityOnThing goes
             through Verb_CastAbility, which is what actually applies the comps below. -->
        <jobDef>CastAbilityOnThing</jobDef>
        <label>riot target</label>
        <description>The Rioter channels Zinc to incite emotion in a single target.

Allies are emboldened, gaining heightened clarity and resolve.
A carefully timed burst against an enemy may stoke fear, anger, or confusion — pushing unstable minds toward a break.</description>
        <metal>Zinc</metal>
        <hediffFriendly>Cosmere_Scadrial_Hediff_RiotedBuff</hediffFriendly>
        <hediffHostile>Cosmere_Scadrial_Hediff_RiotedDebuff</hediffHostile>
        <hediffSeverityFactor>2</hediffSeverityFactor>
        <verbProperties>
            <targetParams>
                <canTargetItems>false</canTargetItems>
                <canTargetBuildings>false</canTargetBuildings>
                <canTargetPlants>false</canTargetPlants>
                <canTargetMechs>false</canTargetMechs>
            </targetParams>
        </verbProperties>
        <maxPower>2</maxPower>
        <!-- Seizing a koloss or a kandra is the same push, aimed at something that can be owned.
             The comp answers with both numbers when the target resists, so the player can see how
             far short they fell and that duralumin closes it. -->
        <comps>
            <!-- The allomantic driver used to spend the metal. Vanilla's does not, so the cost
                 comes back as a comp, the way Steelpush already does it. -->
            <li Class="Cosmere.System.Scadrial.Allomancy.Comp.Ability.MetalCostProperties" />
            <li Class="Cosmere.System.Scadrial.Allomancy.Comp.Ability.InciteBreakProperties" />
            <li Class="Cosmere.System.Scadrial.Allomancy.Comp.Ability.SeizeKolossProperties" />
        </comps>
    </Cosmere.System.Scadrial.Def.AllomanticAbilityDef>
</Defs>